Hi there,

I ran into this a lot too, and wrote a small plugin as a workaround until a proper upstream fix lands.

**What goes wrong** 

The todo list exists in the transcript only at the point where `todowrite` last ran. Forty tool calls later the model is reading the tail of a long turn, and the list is far above it and frequently no longer true.

**What the plugin does** 

Re-states the open items at the tail of every request.

```diff
  user : "do the thing"        <- step 12 of this turn
  asst : todowrite             <- the list was written here, 11 steps back
  asst : read
  asst : edit
  asst : bash
  ...    7 more steps
  asst : grep
+ user : <system-reminder>
+        Your stored todo list:
+        in_progress: refactor the parser
+        pending: update the tests
+        If this no longer matches what you have done, call todowrite now.
+        </system-reminder>
```

The green block is what the plugin appends. It goes at the **tail**, after the newest tool result, because the prompt cache keys on an exact prefix: appending there invalidates almost nothing, whereas editing the original user message re-writes every tool call behind it. It is a user message rather than a part on the assistant message, which would read back as the model's own words.

And it happens on every step, not once:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant OC as OpenCode
    box rgba(46,160,67,0.15)
    participant PL as todo-state.js
    end
    participant LLM as model

    loop every step of the turn
        OC->>PL: experimental.chat.messages.transform(input, output)
        PL->>OC: read session todos
        OC-->>PL: pending + in_progress
        PL-->>OC: output.messages, reminder appended at the tail
        OC->>LLM: request
        LLM-->>OC: tool call or text
        Note over OC,PL: the reminder is discarded with the request,<br/>never written to the database
    end
```

## Workaround

1. Copy the following code into `~/.config/opencode/plugins/todo-state.js`
2. Restart OpenCode

```js
// Re-states a session's todo list on every step. Both OpenCode and Claude Code leave the
// list where the last todowrite put it, which drifts arbitrarily far back in a long turn;
// this puts it back in view. Delete once upstream lands a fix:
//
//   https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/41359  (list goes stale mid-task)
//   https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/27560  (items never marked completed)
//   https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/pull/48729    (fix, closed by a template bot)
//
// Last in the array, after the newest tool result, because a prompt cache keys on an exact
// prefix: there a todo change re-writes only the reminder, where on the last user message
// it re-writes every tool call of the turn behind it. A user message rather than a part on
// the assistant message, which would read back as the model's own words.

const openStatuses = new Set(['pending', 'in_progress']);

const render = todos => {
    const open = todos.filter(todo => openStatuses.has(todo.status));

    if (open.length === 0) {
        return undefined;
    }

    // The wrapper Anthropic models are conditioned to read as out-of-band instruction.
    return ['<system-reminder>',
        'Your stored todo list:',
        ...open.map(todo => `${todo.status}: ${todo.content}`),
        'If this no longer matches what you have done, call todowrite now.',
        '</system-reminder>'].join('\n');
};

// Cloned off a real user message rather than built from scratch, so the request pipeline
// finds every field it reads without this file tracking the Message and Part types.
const textPart = (source, messageID, text) => {
    const template = source.parts.find(part => part.type === 'text') ?? {};

    return { ...template, id: `${messageID}_part`, messageID, type: 'text', text };
};

const reminder = (source, text) => {
    const id = `${source.info.id}_todo_state`;

    return { info: { ...source.info, id }, parts: [textPart(source, id, text)] };
}
